EO:13194,EO:13324,04-1322,Presidential Document,2004-01-20,69 FR 2823,termination,ending,False,True,False,,2,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2004/01/20/04-1322.txt,c06805c2ee9e50f887415c6581bc762ebe037836d03e9f24812cb6a0739129f0,"Pursuant to section 202 of the NEA (50 U.S.C. 1622), termination of the national emergency declared in Executive Order 13194 and expanded in scope in Executive Order 13213 shall not affect any action taken or proceeding pending not finally concluded or determined as of the effective date of this order, or any action or proceeding based on any act committed prior to such date, or any rights or duti"
EO:13197,FRDOC:04-3670,04-3670,Proposed Rule,2004-02-20,69 FR 8030,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,True,2,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2004/02/20/04-3670.txt,9fa41206e8df83763f53acf314f8b7d5c25f6b24c2f475288bb52cbec9a7ac63,"This coordination role is consistent with OPM's institutional responsibility, as codified in 5 U.S.C. chapter 11 and Executive Order 13197 of January 18, 2001, to provide Governmentwide oversight in human resources management programs and practices."
EO:13197,FRDOC:05-1629,05-1629,Rule,2005-02-01,70 FR 5272,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,True,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2005/02/01/05-1629.txt,0f5ddd4df0f231822ea681ca8a73b69981dc4970213542dafa639930e7932252,"The coordination process is intended to give due deference to the flexibilities afforded DHS by the Homeland Security Act and the regulations in this part, without compromising OPM's institutional responsibility, as codified in 5 U.S.C. chapter 11 and Executive Order 13197 of January 18, 2001, to provide Governmentwide oversight in human resources management programs and practices."
