EO:13502,FRDOC:E9-14692,E9-14692,Notice,2009-06-23,74 FR 29900,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2009/06/23/E9-14692.txt,8957d7e73a360b110c75d3908d90abe3cf12fc75cd74eb2297322a0977758b0c,"Appendix 3.4.6 Project Labor Agreements Executive Order 13502, Use of Project Labor Agreements for Federal Construction Projects, issued by President Obama on February 6, 2009, authorizes Federal agencies in awarding any contract in connection with large-scale Federal government construction projects to, on a project- by-project basis, require the use of a project labor agreement by a contractor w"
EO:13502,FRDOC:E9-16617,E9-16617,Rule,2009-07-14,74 FR 34206,amendment,modifying,True,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2009/07/14/E9-16617.txt,ad384e8cdd9b06b2be25c63a81c5418177993537b9e1dcf6e2fbe7c461613e3c,"In accordance with Executive Order 13502--Use of Project Labor Agreements for Federal Construction Projects, this final rule amends FAR 36.202(d) to delete references to the revoked Executive Order 13202."
