EO:13800,FRDOC:2021-24316,2021-24316,Rule,2021-11-08,86 FR 61689,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/11/08/2021-24316.txt,45ff5a53c18253ae157bd9d5ad9b1856b7274241b1f8e19554096e23b6cb8cfc,"Executive Order 13800, Strengthening the Cybersecurity of Federal Networks and Critical Infrastructure (May 2017), directs agency heads to show preference in their procurement for shared information technology (IT) services, to the extent permitted by law, including email, cloud, and cybersecurity services."
