EO:13998,FRDOC:2021-12428,2021-12428,Rule,2021-06-21,86 FR 32376,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/06/21/2021-12428.txt,e36dbd5a7de5fbb7a4d7b0f9016c4f238aa1901b05efd09680b5f37f3f9c6ceb,"And, on January 21, 2021, President Biden issued Executive Order 13998, which recognizes the use of face coverings or facemasks as a necessary, science-based public health measure to prevent the spread of COVID-19, and therefore directed regulatory action to require that they be worn in compliance with CDC guidance while traveling on public transportation (e.g., buses, trains, subway) and while at"
EO:13998,FRDOC:2021-13352,2021-13352,Notice,2021-06-24,86 FR 33473,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/06/24/2021-13352.txt,9d0c50642eecfd2805a5664560068b754d4a50935209a44b4fe1eeb00392b120,"On January 21, 2021, President Biden issued Executive Order 13998 titled ``Promoting COVID-19 Safety in Domestic and International Travel'' ``to save lives and allow all Americans, including the millions of people employed in the transportation industry, to travel and work safely,'' requiring immediate Federal action to mandate masks on public forms of transportation, including transit."
